- Story & Context: The foreman, a man named Silas who refused to climb the lift, spent his final hours measuring the heartbeat of the rock with a rhythmic, percussive piano riff. He claimed he could hear the ventilation pipes singing back in a tongue that predated the excavation of the tunnels. His colleagues found him unconscious, his hands raw from striking the keys so hard they bled onto the ivory. "Don't you recognize the sound of the earth breathing through your teeth?"
