Track 3: The After-Postmark
- Story & Context: Decades later, the shaft is sealed, yet local hikers often report hearing a faint, melodic clanging emanating from the ground whenever a storm front approaches. They call it the 'Postmark Ghost,' a myth about a lost message that eventually turns into a song once the paper has fully rotted away. A young girl once placed her ear to the ventilation grate and heard the piano’s final, lingering chord vibrating through the entire mountain. "We are only the notes written on the inside of the stone."
